iDroidik — Android on iPhone 7 — third-party components and attribution
=====================================================================

This project is a thin orchestration + patch layer on top of other people's
hard work. It bundles or builds on the following, each under its OWN license
(which governs those files — the project's own MIT license at the bottom does
NOT override them). If you redistribute this project, keep this NOTICE.

Project Sandcastle / linux-sandcastle (Corellium)  —  GPL-2.0
  Android/Linux for the iPhone; the 5.4 kernel, loaders, touch daemon (hx-touchd),
  syscfg/hcd extraction tools, and the AOSP build diff.
  Source: https://github.com/corellium/projectsandcastle
          https://github.com/corellium/linux-sandcastle  (kernel — GPL-2.0; full
          source is the linux-sandcastle tree, not vendored here)
          https://github.com/corellium/sandcastle-buildroot
  Vendored here under: psc/, linux/, android-sandcastle/, loader/ (modified).
  License: GPL-2.0 — see psc/LICENSE. The loaders in loader/ (pongo-bootr,
  pongo-linux, pongo-shell) are derived from Corellium's load-linux.c.
  GPL-2.0 corresponding source for the built kernel (work/Image-a16f.lzma):
    base   = corellium/linux-sandcastle @ commit 0c2f7dda13d67bb7e06123df516f8bdb1000a79b
             (Linux 5.4.14)
    patch  = kernel-patches/idroidik-linux-sandcastle-5.4.14.patch (our changes to
             binder.c, kernel/bpf/cgroup.c, drivers/power/reset/hx-reboot.c)
    config = work/android16-kernel.config ; toolchain = gcc 7.5 (kbuild7/Dockerfile)
  Clone the base at that commit, `git apply` the patch, build with that config — see
  docs/BUILD.md. If you redistribute the kernel binary, ship these alongside it.

mxml (Michael R Sweet)  —  Apache-2.0 (with static-linking exception)
  XML parser bundled inside the touch daemon.
  Vendored here under: psc/hx-touchd/mxml-3.1/
  Source: https://github.com/michaelrsweet/mxml

libimobiledevice (iproxy, libplist, libusbmuxd)  —  LGPL-2.1
  USB/lockdown helpers shipped with the original Sandcastle macOS tooling.
  Vendored here under: android-sandcastle/iproxy, android-sandcastle/libplist.3.dylib,
  android-sandcastle/libusbmuxd.4.dylib
  Source: https://github.com/libimobiledevice

PongoOS (checkra1n team)  —  MIT
  Pre-boot execution environment used to load the kernel over checkm8.
  Source: https://github.com/checkra1n/PongoOS
  Vendored here under: pongo/  (License: MIT — see pongo/LICENSE.md)

palera1n
  checkm8 jailbreak / boot tool used to run the exploit and enter pongoOS.
  https://palera.in — NOT redistributed here; the user installs it themselves.

SwiftShader (Google)  —  Apache-2.0
  CPU implementation of Vulkan; built into the vulkan.pastel.so software GPU
  driver this project ships as a build recipe (docs/BUILD.md).
  Source: https://github.com/google/swiftshader

TrebleDroid GSI / Android Open Source Project (Google + TrebleDroid)  —  Apache-2.0
  The Android 16 system image (GSI) that runs on top of the kernel.
  https://github.com/TrebleDroid/treble_experimentations
  NOT redistributed in this git repo; fetched/built per MANIFEST.md.

Apple Inc. firmware (touch, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, syscfg)
  REQUIRED at runtime but NEVER redistributed by this project. It is extracted
  on the user's own device from their own licensed iOS. See
  docs/FIRMWARE-AND-LEGAL.md.

The name "iDroidik" is used in homage to the original iDroid / openiBoot project
(2010–2012, Android on the early iPhones); this is an independent, unrelated effort.

